$ Python standard library: socket.makefile
@ socket.makefile

`sock.makefile()` returns a *file object* associated with the socket.

The socket must be in blocking mode.

Closing the object returned by `makefile()` does not  close the original socket *unless* all other file objects have been closed and `close() ` has also been called on the socket object.

